{"body":"Edit Dose's trash is now red like Edit Entry's, and this PR states who places Log Dose's title.\n\n### Problem\n\nThe app-wide tint paints a toolbar button in the brand colour, so `role: .destructive` alone left Edit Dose's trash\nbrand-coloured while Edit Entry's was red. The catalog line for `destructive` says not to rely on the role alone.\n\n### Change\n\nOne line in `App/EditDose/EditDoseView.swift`: `.tint(Color.destructive)` on the \"Delete dose\" button, in the same\nplace Edit Entry has it. Position, capsule, confirmation and the spoken \"Delete dose\" are unchanged.\n\n### Log Dose title\n\nThe system placed the Log Dose title, no code of ours did, and design accepts the leading title. `git grep -n principal -- App`\nfinds only New Entry placing a title by hand:\n\n```\nApp/NewEntry/NewEntryView.swift:110:                ToolbarItem(placement: .principal) {\n```\n\n### Look check\n\nNo design picture in the brief. The reference is Edit Entry's trash, compared by eye in light and dark.\n\n| Control | Design (Edit Entry) | Mine (Edit Dose) | Match |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Trash colour, light | system red | system red | yes |\n| Trash colour, dark | system red | system red | yes |\n| Capsule | own glass capsule left of the filled check | same | yes |\n| Size | 36 pt button | 36 pt button | yes |\n\n### Walk on a fresh simulator, seed `spread`\n\n- History, newest day (Yesterday) holds a dose. `dose-row` opens Edit Dose and its trash is red in its own capsule left\n  of the check.\n- `delete-dose` opens the confirmation. The button reads `AXLabel: Delete dose`, `AXButton`, frame 36 x 36.\n- An entry from History opens Edit Entry and its trash is the same red.\n\n### Shared pieces\n\nUsed `Color.destructive` from the catalog. No new piece.\n"}
